# Trivy ignore file — accepted, non-applicable, or out-of-scope findings.
#
# Every Trivy step in .github/workflows also sets `ignore-unfixed: true`, which
# already drops CVEs with no upstream fix. Only fixable-but-deliberately-accepted
# CVEs belong here, each justified. IDs are global (apply to every image).
# Review on every base-image bump.

# --- Apache Derby (bundled inside the pyspark wheel) ---
# CVE-2022-46337 is an LDAP-auth bypass in Derby's *network server*. This
# pipeline uses Spark as an embedded local engine only; the Derby network
# server and its LDAP auth path are never started. Revisit if a Hive metastore
# backed by Derby is ever introduced.
CVE-2022-46337
